    "result_text": "Tests remain green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 run / 0 failures).\n\n## Outcome\n\nI reviewed both findings and respectfully disagree with both; no changes made.\n\n1. **Transaction governance on `audit`** \u2014 The finding assumes `respond` omits `govern: [ transaction ]`, but it carries it (verified, lines 67\u201369). The whole `build`\u2192`respond` chain is one contiguous governed span (respond needs the open transaction for lazy DTO mapping). `audit` is in the *middle* of that span, so removing governance wouldn't shorten the transaction \u2014 respond keeps it open either way \u2014 it would only violate AGENTS.md's \"listed on **every** step it covers\" rule by leaving a gap. Keeping it is the consistent and correct choice.\n\n2. **`service` \u2192 `audit` rename** \u2014 The codebase's real convention (all 25 owner functions) is a single `service` method; only the AGENTS.md illustration uses verb names. Renaming would make this class the lone outlier among its siblings. The verb already lives in the class name `AuditOwnerCreated`.\n\nAcceptance behaviour is unchanged and the suite is green.",
